# V1.0.1 — Matching Calibration + Strategic Decision Layer

Goal:
Improve the deterministic matching engine so it is more transparent, more useful, and closer to strategic grant judgment — without adding AI APIs.

Do not add OpenAI/OpenRouter/Anthropic.
Do not add native AI calls.
Do not scrape.
Do not add autonomous agents.
Do not redesign the dashboard.
Do not weaken RLS.
Do not break existing matching behavior.
Do not require the full real dataset to be present.

Build a calibration and decision layer on top of the existing rules engine.

---

## 1. Add Strategic Decision Label

The match tier alone is not enough.

Add a new field to `grant_matches`:

`decision_label text not null default 'needs_review'`

Allowed values:
- apply_now
- prepare_next
- monitor
- skip
- track_next_cycle
- needs_review

Add a human-readable label in UI:
- Apply Now
- Prepare Next
- Monitor
- Skip
- Track Next Cycle
- Needs Review

Decision logic should consider:
- match score
- readiness score
- urgency score
- deadline status
- eligibility risk
- data completeness
- whether deadline has passed
- whether deadline is too close with low readiness

Example logic:
- High match + enough readiness + deadline active/soon = Apply Now
- High match + low readiness + deadline not too close = Prepare Next
- Medium match + later/rolling deadline = Monitor
- Past deadline = Track Next Cycle or Skip depending fit
- Low match + strong eligibility/geography mismatch = Skip
- Missing key fields = Needs Review

Do not make this perfect. Make it transparent and practical.

