3. Improve Deadline Language + Deadline Strategy

Fix wording:

Current bad wording:

“Ending in 0 days”

Replace with:

Due today
Past due by X days
X days left
Rolling deadline
Deadline unknown

Decision behavior:

Deadline passed → Track Next Cycle or Skip
Due today + high readiness → Apply Now
Due today + low readiness → Too Late / Needs Review
1–7 days + low readiness → Prepare only if already drafted
8–30 days + strong match → Apply Now or Prepare Next
31–60 days → Prepare Next / Monitor
rolling → Monitor / Prepare Next depending score
unknown → Needs Review

Add this deadline status to fit reasons/risks/recommended actions.

4. Improve Readiness Score

Current readiness can be too harsh or unclear.

Readiness should consider:

project profile completeness
proof items linked to project
public proof items
linked documents
extracted document text
applications already started
tasks completed/open
agent notes/reports
presence of application materials like problem statement, solution, impact, budget, team, demo/screenshots, metrics, legal/eligibility notes if represented in available fields

Suggested readiness logic:

project profile fields complete: up to 20 points
proof items: up to 25 points
documents/extracted text: up to 15 points
application workspace exists/progress: up to 15 points
tasks completed / low blockers: up to 10 points
agent notes/reports: up to 10 points
eligibility/legal/budget evidence if detectable: up to 5 points

Then normalize to 0–100.

Do not require all fields to exist. Use whatever data is available safely.

Add missing items when readiness is low:

Add proof items
Add demo/screenshots
Add impact metrics
Add budget narrative
Confirm legal applicant / fiscal sponsor
Draft reusable application answers
Add project brief
Attach grant guidelines/document
